From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] oledb32: DBTYPE_NUMERIC as conversion source (3663)

oledb32: DBTYPE_NUMERIC as conversion source

IDataConvert::DataConvert accepted DBTYPE_NUMERIC in CanConvert but failed
with E_NOTIMPL for every numeric, currency, boolean, date and string
destination. The source is now converted through DECIMAL (a DB_NUMERIC
magnitude above 96 bits or a scale above 28 is an overflow).
---
diff --git a/dlls/oledb32/convert.c b/dlls/oledb32/convert.c
index 540ceac..d8ee482 100644
--- a/dlls/oledb32/convert.c
+++ b/dlls/oledb32/convert.c
@@ -154,6 +154,22 @@ static int get_length(DBTYPE type)
     }
 }
 
+/* DB_NUMERIC holds a 128-bit little endian magnitude, DECIMAL a 96-bit one. */
+static HRESULT numeric_to_decimal(const void *src, DECIMAL *dec)
+{
+    const DB_NUMERIC *n = src;
+
+    if (n->val[12] || n->val[13] || n->val[14] || n->val[15]) return DISP_E_OVERFLOW;
+    if (n->scale > 28) return DISP_E_OVERFLOW;
+    memset(dec, 0, sizeof(*dec));
+    dec->scale = n->scale;
+    dec->sign = n->sign ? 0 : DECIMAL_NEG;
+    memcpy(&dec->Lo32, n->val, 4);
+    memcpy(&dec->Mid32, n->val + 4, 4);
+    memcpy(&dec->Hi32, n->val + 8, 4);
+    return S_OK;
+}
+
